@startuml
title Figure 10 — UML Deployment diagram — packaged runtime and optional external nodes
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 55

node "Operator device" as Device <<device>> {
  artifact "Web browser" as Browser
}

node "Docker Compose / Linux host" as Host <<executionEnvironment>> {
  node "application service / container" as App <<executionEnvironment>> {
    node "embedded Tomcat 11" as Tomcat <<executionEnvironment>> {
      artifact "React static assets\nclasspath /static" as React
      artifact "Spring MVC /api/*" as Api
    }
    artifact "Spring Boot executable JAR" as Jar
    artifact "Offline adapters\nStaticPolicyAdapter +\nDeterministicAnalysisStub" as Offline
  }

  node "database service / container\nR2+ when activated" as DB <<database>> {
    artifact "PostgreSQL + pgvector" as PostgreSQL
  }
}

node "External AI provider\noptional later-ring adapter" as Provider <<external>>

Browser --> Tomcat : HTTP :8080\nhost-published application port
Tomcat --> React : static /
Tomcat --> Api : in-process /api/*
Jar --> Tomcat : packaged runtime
Api --> DB : JDBC / PostgreSQL\nTCP 5432 private network when activated
Api ..> Provider : HTTPS provider API\nonly when explicitly configured
Api --> Offline : in-process mandatory baseline path

note bottom of Host
  R0/R1 reviewer packaging exposes one application container and one browser-facing port.
  React is compiled before runtime and served from the executable JAR by embedded Tomcat.
  PostgreSQL and the external provider activate only in later rings when configured.
  TLS termination, ingress, load balancing, and public DNS remain deployment-profile concerns.
end note
@enduml
